  -o build/repro/after-o2.ll
```

Create build/repro and place your actual reproducer there first. These paths are an example workspace, not files already generated by the book.

### Verify

After fixing the mistake, the narrow regression must turn green, and the existing relevant suite must remain green. Remove the fault injection. Keep an assertion on the root cause as well as the behavioral case when practical.

<details>
<summary>LLVM IR — Why optimization exposes earlier mistakes</summary>

A dominance violation or false preservation claim may survive a simple code path and fail only when another pass consumes the bad information. The last pass before a crash is not automatically responsible. Find the earliest broken invariant and reduce to that boundary rather than disabling optimization as the final fix.

